      "id": "reg-m2-tbs3-ex1",
      "title": "Business facts",
      "html": "<p>A member signs a personal guarantee. A business labels workers contractors while controlling their daily work. A director secretly takes an entity opportunity. A consultant is paid to pass money improperly to a foreign official.</p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "reg-m2-tbs3-ex2",
      "title": "Instructions",
      "html": "<p>Identify the issue rather than assuming a legal label determines the outcome. No special statutory exception is stated.</p>"
    }
  ],
  "explanation": "<h3>Guarantee issue</h3><p>The guarantee can bind the owner personally.</p><h3>Worker issue</h3><p>Classification requires substantive analysis.</p><h3>Director issue</h3><p>Secret personal diversion creates a loyalty concern.</p><h3>Payment issue</h3><p>Intermediary use does not make an improper payment lawful.</p>"
